      "content": "I'm so sorry you're feeling this heavy sense of hopelessness, and it's completely understandable to feel exhausted when things feel inescapable. Even though the weight you carry might feel permanent, feelings of being \"just past the point\" are common during deep depression and can be a sign of burnout rather than a final end. You deserve support to explore whether there might be help that can ease that weight, and please consider reaching out to a mental health professional or a trusted person you can talk to.",
